  "details": "Avatar haptics will trigger in strange locations around a imposter and causes \"Random\" haptics.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n1) Enable avatar haptics.\n\n2) Turn on contact debug. (Optional)\n\n3) Show the avatar as an imposter.\n\n4) Hover around the model and feel the haptics.\n\nBellow is an image of were the haptics were activating on my controller.\n\nThe problem goes away when you show the avatar.\n\n<Amendment>\n\nI have been informed that avatar haptics do not use contacts. Regardless the bug still occurs.",
